    {
      "filename": "Bedroom (35873114146).jpg",
      "title": "File:Bedroom (35873114146).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/Bedroom_%2835873114146%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bedroom_(35873114146).jpg",
      "width": 6000,
      "height": 4000,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Dennis G. Jarvis",
      "description": "A bedroom in the house of Antoine Rodrigue.\n\nAntoine Rodrigue, was a  ship’s captain, merchant, and colonial official at Louisbourg in 1722.\nHis business activities started before the siege of Louisbourg in 1745. By 1752 he had established himself in Louisbourg and had a house built there on the corner of the Rue Saint-Louis and the Rue d’ Orléans. His black slave was baptized in Louisbourg on 9 Feb. 1754. \nAfter the taking of the fortress in 1758, Rodrigue was sent back to France, being exchanged as a prisoner of war. He probably never came back to North America, remaining instead in France. \n\nAntoine had married Jeanne-Françoise Jacau, on 19 May 1750; they had at least nine children.",
      "dateCreated": "2017-06-14 12:32",
      "categories": [
        "Bedrooms in Nova Scotia",
        "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
